 const v=await evaluate(()=>getApp().globalData.application.render().teaching),criterion=v.lesson.rubric[0],anchor=v.lesson.roleAnchors[criterion.id][0];await action('criterion',criterion.id);await tap('[data-action="studio-link"][data-value="'+criterion.id+':'+anchor+'"]');await nativeField('studioAfter',(id==='l-w-advice'?"Hi Sam, It can be hard to know where to begin. First, choose four useful words each day and use them in short sentences. This can help you understand how the words work. Second, read one short paragraph and write down a question about it. A small task can be easier to keep doing, and your teacher can help with the question. You do not need to learn everything at once. Start today and give yourself time to improve. Best wishes, A friend":(id==='l-w-notice'?"BOOK EXCHANGE Come to the school gate this Saturday from nine to eleven in the morning. All students are welcome. Please bring a book you have finished reading and check that it is in good condition. Put it on the exchange table, then choose another book to enjoy at home. Do not bring books with torn covers or damaged pages. You can tell another student why you enjoyed your book. Let us give our old books a new reader!":(id==='l-w-story'?"A small act of kindness\nAfter lunch, I noticed a new student standing outside our classroom. He was looking for the science room, but he did not know the way. I had a few minutes before my next lesson, so I offered to walk there with him. We checked the room sign together, and he smiled with relief. He thanked me before going inside. I felt pleased because a little of my time had made his day easier. The experience reminded me to notice when someone nearby needs help.":(id==='l-w-opinion'?"I do not support setting aside a fixed fifteen-minute reading block every day. First, students have different learning needs, so some may need that time to finish another important task. Second, a fixed block may not suit everyone\u2019s reading pace; some students would prefer a longer session on fewer days. I understand the worry that students may seldom read without a regular time. We could offer optional reading sessions and help everyone make a personal plan instead. This would encourage regular reading while leaving room for different needs. We should review the arrangement with classmates after a short trial.":(id==='l-w-report'?"During the lunch break, our class checked how water was being used around the school. We noticed two taps that had not been turned off properly. The water-saving notice at the library entrance was also hard to see. Classmates were willing to take turns checking the taps. We suggest putting a clearer notice in a place students can easily see. We could also ask willing volunteers to check the taps before leaving the area. These are proposed changes, so we should discuss the arrangements first and then review whether they help us spot problems sooner.":(id==='l-s-introduce'?"I enjoy growing herbs in small pots. Each morning, I check the soil and water the plants if they need it. I also turn the pots so the leaves get enough light. I like watching new leaves appear and using the herbs in our meals. It feels good to look after something and see it grow.":(id==='l-s-retell'?"On Saturday, my friend and I visited a park. We noticed litter beside a bench and began to clear it away. We kept different kinds of rubbish separate as we worked. Later, a visitor came over and helped us. I felt encouraged because someone else wanted to join in. The experience showed me that a small helpful action can invite another person to help too.":(id==='l-s-plan'?"Could we meet in the classroom at three this Sunday afternoon to make our English poster? I can bring some pictures, and you could bring paper and pens. First, we can choose the main points together. I could write short captions while you arrange the pictures. Then we can check the English and the layout together. What do you think of this plan? Please tell me if you would like to change anything.":(id==='l-s-compare'?"My school is about three kilometres from home. Cycling gives me some exercise, while taking the bus can be useful in bad weather. Today I would choose the bus because heavy rain is expected. I would check the service information before leaving. On a dry day, I might prefer to cycle. Neither way is always the best for everyone; my choice depends on the weather and traffic for this particular journey.\n":(id==='l-s-opinion'?"I do not think the same student should always speak for our group. Taking turns gives everyone useful practice. It also allows us to hear ideas from different members. Before an activity, we could each prepare one point and help the next speaker rehearse. If someone is worried about making mistakes, we could try this arrangement once and discuss how it went. We should improve the plan together rather than criticise a classmate.\n":(id==='l-s-problem'?"Excuse me, I borrowed this book on Monday and noticed some missing pages while reading this afternoon. Without those pages, I cannot understand how the experiment ends. I do not know what caused the damage. Could I exchange the book for another copy, please? I would like to finish reading the explanation.\n":(id==='l-s-read-aloud'?"I will keep half past four together, read the library door clearly and leave a natural pause between the question and its reply. After reading both roles aloud, I will record and listen for missing words, then practise unclear phrases again.\n":(id==='l-w-note'?"Hi Ben,\nWould you like to visit the park with me this Saturday? Let us meet at the school gate at ten in the morning. Please remember to bring a bottle of water. I hope we can enjoy a pleasant morning together.\nSee you,\nAlex\n":(id==='l-s-course-t01'?"I have basketball practice after school on Wednesday. I will read a short story on the bus home instead. This change lets me make time for reading without missing practice.\n":(id==='l-w-course-t01'?"I have basketball practice after school on Wednesday. I will read during the journey home instead because I still want to enjoy a story that day. This change helps me keep both activities in my plan.\n":(id==='l-s-course-t02'?"The garden club meets at four on Tuesday. Please come to the green gate. Listen to the teacher\u2019s instructions before using any tools.\n":(id==='l-w-course-t02'?"Our garden club meets at four on Tuesday. We will meet by the green gate, not the main school gate. Before using any tools, please listen to the teacher\u2019s instructions.\n":(id==='l-s-course-t03'?"I am worried about our class talk because I do not know how to begin. Could I speak to you privately after the lesson? I would like some help planning the first few steps.\n":(id==='l-w-course-t03'?"I am worried about speaking in front of my class because I cannot organise my opening ideas. Would it be possible to talk with you privately after the lesson? I would like some help deciding how to begin.\n":(id==='l-s-course-t04'?"I will close my notes and try to write the five words from memory. Then I will check my answers against the notes. Copying while looking would not show what I can recall on my own.\n":(id==='l-w-course-t04'?"I will close my notes and try to write the five words from memory. I will check my notes after I have made my attempt. Copying while looking cannot show what I can recall on my own.\n":(id==='l-s-course-t05'?"My bag is untidy today, but that does not mean I can never organise things. I can begin by putting the papers I need tomorrow together in one pocket. This is a small change I can start today.\n":(id==='l-w-course-t05'?"My bag is untidy today, but that does not mean I can never organise things. I can begin by putting tomorrow\u2019s papers together in one pocket. This is a small change I can start today.\n":(id==='l-s-course-t06'?"She works with the stage props behind the scenes. She prepares the objects on the list and puts them back after the show. These jobs help the actors use the right props when they need them.":(id==='l-w-course-t06'?"She is responsible for preparing the stage props on the list. She also returns them to their places after the show. Her work behind the scenes helps the actors find the objects they need.":(id==='l-s-course-t07'?"I have watered the class plant, but I still need to clean up. I will wipe the shelf and put the bottle back. Leaving the corner ready for the next person is part of finishing the task.":(id==='l-w-course-t07'?"I have watered the class plant, but I still need to finish the cleanup. I will wipe the shelf and return the bottle. This will leave the corner ready for the next person to use.":(id==='l-s-course-t08'?"The three-pack costs five yuan per notebook, but fifteen yuan in total. I have twelve yuan and need only one notebook today. I will buy the six-yuan one and have six yuan left.":(id==='l-w-course-t08'?"The three-pack costs less per notebook, but it costs fifteen yuan in total. I have twelve yuan and need only one notebook today, so I will buy the six-yuan one. I will have six yuan left.":(id==='l-s-course-t09'?"Our labels keep falling off, but we do not know the cause yet. We should first record which corners or edges come loose. Those observations can help us consider possible causes before replacing every label or blaming the tape.":(id==='l-w-course-t09'?"Our labels often fall off, but we have not checked the cause yet. We should observe where they come loose and record what happens. Those records can help us consider possible causes before judging the tape.":(id==='l-s-course-t10'?"I thought you no longer wanted to play with me when you left the game. Now I know you needed to pick up your younger sister. I should have asked you first instead of guessing.":(id==='l-w-course-t10'?"I thought you were angry with me when you left the game. Now I know you needed to pick up your younger sister. I should have asked you first instead of guessing.":(id==='l-s-course-t11'?"I will wash the vegetables on Monday, and my brother will set the table. If I cannot do my part, I will tell the family before the work begins.":(id==='l-w-course-t11'?"I will wash the vegetables on Monday, and my brother will set the table. If I cannot do my part, I will tell the family before the work needs to begin.":(id==='l-s-course-t12'?"The event begins at ten on Sunday, but volunteers should arrive at nine forty-five. We need to listen to the introduction so we understand our roles before the event begins.":(id==='l-w-course-t12'?"The event begins at ten on Sunday, but volunteers should arrive at nine forty-five. We need time for the introduction so that we understand our roles before the event begins.":(id==='l-s-course-t13'?"I will check the guide\u2019s wording, and my partner will ask the makers for permission. Both jobs matter because a clear guide should also respect the people whose work it describes.":(id==='l-w-course-t13'?"I will check the guide\u2019s wording, and my partner will ask the makers for permission. Both jobs matter because a clear guide should also respect the people whose work it describes.":(id==='l-s-course-t14'?"The fictional station room once stored tools. It now displays neighbourhood photographs. The display can help people compare changes, but not every change is an improvement.":(id==='l-w-course-t14'?"People used to store tools in this fictional station room. It now displays neighborhood photographs. The display may help people compare changes, but not every change is an improvement.":"Hi Alex, Would you like to come to our school reading club this Friday? We are meeting in the library at 4 p.m. Please bring a book you enjoy. You can tell us about an interesting character and listen to other students' ideas. We will also recommend books to each other. You do not have to prepare a long talk. Please reply to tell me whether you can attend. I hope to see you there. Best wishes, A friend"))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))));for(const point of v.lesson.revisionRubric)await tap('[data-action="studio-rubric"][data-value="'+point.id+'"]');await tap('[data-action="studio-review"]');await shot('revision-self-check');checks.push('SDK-triggered planning cards preserve fixed invitation facts, retain drafts across route changes and support actual revision/self-check bindings')
